99b7c6e:CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY.md:52:- `ELISTLY_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` = comma-separated exact frontend origins permitted to make credentialed browser API requests, for example `https://app.example.test,https://preview.example.test`.
99b7c6e:DOCS.md:124:Import previews and merges the current top-level selective inventory format. It does not yet restore the full-account export envelope. Validate important restores on disposable data until the versioned round-trip format in the roadmap is complete.
99b7c6e:DOCS.md:168:Elistly is designed as an installable browser app. The service worker and manifest support PWA-style use where browser support allows it.
99b7c6e:README.md:23:- **Windows Device Intake** — Settings → Data → Device Intake provides a disclosed local-only collector download, bounded report validation, conflict-aware preview, and confirmed import. The collector needs no administrator access and performs no network or directory lookup.
99b7c6e:README.md:50:For a complete reference—concepts, current behavior, deployment, and project structure—see **[DOCS.md](DOCS.md)**. Planned work is tracked in **[ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md)**, including the recovered **[Windows Device Intake plan](WINDOWS_DEVICE_INTAKE_PLAN.md)**.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:33:- Reliable service-worker update behavior after backend/frontend changes.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:35:- Windows Device Intake.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:42:- [ ] **Revision-aware persistence** — Replace blind whole-document last-writer-wins updates with an explicit revision/ETag contract and conflict response.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:48:## P0 – Windows Device Intake
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:52:- [ ] **Versioned local collector** — Collect a disclosed, bounded set of Windows hardware, OS, and account facts without administrator access or default network calls.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:53:- [ ] **Strict report contract** — Validate `elistly.device-intake.v1`, enforce size/depth/type limits, and reject unsupported schemas before creating a preview.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:54:- [ ] **Side-effect-free preview** — Show exact create/update changes without mutating schema, dropdowns, entities, or persisted data.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:58:- [ ] **Checksummed candidate package** — Record exact collector path, checksum, contents, and launch instructions before asking for real-machine testing.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:76:- [ ] **CSV import** — Map columns to one entity type, preview validation, then bulk-create through the authoritative mutation path.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:99:- [ ] **Normalized ownership/revision design** — Define list/category/item ownership, permissions, revisions, and migration from existing payloads.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:102:- [ ] **Activity log** — Record who changed what, when, and from which prior revision.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:112:- Windows Device Intake is now a first-class P0 requirement with its own contract and acceptance plan.
99b7c6e:ROADMAP.md:117:- Whether collaboration justifies normalizing the entire persistence model beyond revision-safe single-user storage.
99b7c6e:SECURITY.md:3:Elistly is publicly hosted and its source repository is public. Treat every tracked filename and every reachable Git revision as public information.
99b7c6e:SECURITY.md:35:- revision-aware persistence and durable failed-write handling;
99b7c6e:SECURITY.md:37:- bounded, privacy-preserving Windows Device Intake.
99b7c6e:VERDICT.md:8:- Import preview now builds all data-bearing preview nodes with DOM APIs and `textContent`; checkbox identity and selection use properties rather than interpolated attributes.
99b7c6e:VERDICT.md:17:- `01-import-preview-red.txt`: baseline browser FileReader/JSON.parse/import-preview regression failed as expected: nine attacker-created IMG/SVG/SCRIPT nodes.
99b7c6e:VERDICT.md:18:- `02-import-preview-green.txt` and `07-final-import-runtime.txt`: real file-input import of hostile labels, entity content, hostile object keys, quote/attribute markup, entity-encoded markup, Unicode, nested data, and script markup passed. It verified literal text, no active preview IMG/SVG/SCRIPT, no handler execution, correct category/type/entity checkbox values, and selected-data localStorage persistence.
99b7c6e:WINDOWS_DEVICE_INTAKE_PLAN.md:1:# Windows Device Intake
99b7c6e:WINDOWS_DEVICE_INTAKE_PLAN.md:7:Let an authorized user collect inventory facts from a Windows computer, preview them in Elistly, and deliberately create or update a computer record and its assigned person.
99b7c6e:WINDOWS_DEVICE_INTAKE_PLAN.md:13:1. The user downloads or copies the versioned Elistly Windows collector.
99b7c6e:WINDOWS_DEVICE_INTAKE_PLAN.md:14:2. Before collection, the collector states exactly which local fields it reads and whether optional directory enrichment is enabled.
99b7c6e:WINDOWS_DEVICE_INTAKE_PLAN.md:15:3. The collector runs without administrator privileges and creates one versioned JSON report in a location chosen by the user.
99b7c6e:WINDOWS_DEVICE_INTAKE_PLAN.md:16:4. The user opens **Settings → Data → Device Intake** and selects or pastes that report.
99b7c6e:WINDOWS_DEVICE_INTAKE_PLAN.md:20:8. Only **Confirm import** may change data. The report records and disclosed additive schema changes are saved as one coherent revision-aware change. A failed pre-commit save restores the previous local state; a successful remote save followed by a local-cache failure must instead report that the remote commit succeeded and require reload.
